# URLs lychee should not check. One regex per line.
#
# Only add a host here when it is *reachable in a browser but unverifiable by
# a bot* — aggressive WAFs, login walls, or hard bot blocks. Never add a host
# to silence a genuinely dead link; fix or remove the entry instead.

# --- Social platforms: block non-browser agents outright ---
^https?://(www\.)?linkedin\.com/
^https?://(www\.)?x\.com/
^https?://(twitter\.com|t\.co)/
^https?://(www\.)?reddit\.com/

# --- Standards bodies behind bot protection / paywalls ---
^https?://(www\.)?iso\.org/

# --- Vendor sites with aggressive WAFs that 403/406 CI traffic ---
# uber.com returns 406 Not Acceptable to non-browser agents; the linked
# engineering posts are reachable normally.
^https?://(www\.)?uber\.com/
^https?://(www\.)?oracle\.com/
^https?://(www\.)?salesforce\.com/
^https?://(www\.)?servicenow\.com/
^https?://(www\.)?klarna\.com/
^https?://(www\.)?gartner\.com/

# --- TEMPORARY: remove once the repo has its first star and watcher ---
# GitHub returns 404 for /stargazers and /watchers while those counts are
# zero. These are badge targets, not content links, and start working on
# their own. Delete these two lines once the counts are non-zero.
^https?://github\.com/seyhunak/awesome-ai/stargazers$
^https?://github\.com/seyhunak/awesome-ai/watchers$

# --- Rendered dynamically; the checker sees an empty shell ---
^https?://api\.star-history\.com/
^https?://img\.shields\.io/

# --- Local and example URLs ---
^https?://(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1)
^https?://example\.(com|org)
